\section{Choosing the arguments}{

\code{n_iter = 2000}, \code{burn = 200}, \code{thin = 10}, the \eqn{IG(0.1, 0.1)} prior on the
residual variance, \code{c0 = d0 = v = 1} and \code{a_model = b_model = 1} are the settings of
the authors' code. \code{estimator = "median"} ranks by the posterior median; \code{"mean"} ranks
by the posterior mean. \code{K = NULL} evaluates the full path, whose cost per node is
cubic in \code{K}; a smaller \code{K} saves time when neighbourhoods are known to be small.
}

\section{Parallel computing}{

Each node has its own seed, \code{seed + a}, so a fit with a given \code{seed} is identical for
every value of \code{cores}. Workers need the package to be installed. When \code{cores > 1},
limit the threads of a multi-threaded BLAS so that they do not compete with the
workers.
}

